// Self-centered fey-majesty aura, same `pooled_debuff` GroundAoe shape as
// sleep.ron (a self/near-self AoE that resolves once at cast, granting its
// buff to everyone caught in range rather than dealing a normal hit).
// Sheet rider is "prone-and-pushed (awe) OR charmed, plus minor psychic
// damage" -- `BuffKind::Charmed` was checked and rejected: it resolves to
// an empty effects list for player-controlled/most targets
// (`common/src/comp/buff.rs` ~line 1209, `Charmed | Dominated | Maddened =>
// vec![]`) -- it's an NPC-alignment-flip marker, not a real player-facing
// debuff, so it would do nothing here. `Rooted` (can't move) stands in for
// "cowed/held by awe" instead, the same substitution already used
// elsewhere in this pass for "held in place" riders. The minor-damage half
// is dropped: `pooled_debuff` fully replaces the strike's normal damage
// path (see GroundAoe's own doc comment), so a real hit and a pooled debuff
// can't coexist on one cast.
GroundAoe(
    energy_cost: 80.0,
    buildup_duration: 0.5,
    delay: 0.4,
    recover_duration: 0.4,
    max_range: 3.0,
    radius: 3.0,
    min_falloff: 0.4,
    damage: 0.0,
    poise: 0.0,
    knockback: (strength: 0.0, direction: Away),
    dodgeable: No,
    reagent: None,
    rooted_cast: true,
    pooled_debuff: Some((
        pool: 60.0,
        buff: (
            kind: Rooted,
            dur_secs: 8,
            strength: Value(1.0),
            chance: 1.0,
        ),
    )),
    meta: (
        school: Some(Enchantment),
        source: Some(Arcane),
        // level 5 spell -> min_level 30, the level * 6 convention.
        requirements: (min_level: Some(30)),
    ),
)
